# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-2, 2.1-4). L §2.3: kline = "owned" "by" ID [tieby] | "batched" | "step" UNIT | "takes" ID
# "for" ID ["v" ID] ("order" expr {"," expr} ["prorata" [tieby]] | "prorata" [tieby]) | ...; place = ... "lives" lspan
# NL {IN "note" STR NL}; balx ... ["of" ofq]; valuex ... ["by" ...] ["of" ofq]; post ... ["." FIELD "of" ofq]; row =
# qid [rowkeys] ["of" ofrow] "=" .... L §2.4: "A one-line def followed by note lines means the long form, the same def
# with its one rule labelled base and those notes, and prints as it" (arrive); "Parentheses appear only where
# precedence needs them" (the order's first term and the ties by keep theirs: tieby takes one term, parse rule 7; the
# if after `order` loses its pair, as `(if ...)` alone does in L2_4_reprint_expressions); a kind's lines are one
# repeated choice, kept in file order (canon's BODY_RANK); kinds in tree order, persons (under the prelude's parties)
# among the roots (GD-9); a place's notes follow its line. A reading's part row sorts
# beside its total by GD-28's ASCII tie ("stated[konto] = ..." before "stated[konto] of ...").
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind savings: place one min 0
  note "a joint account"
  owned by arrive ties by (if p == ania then 0 else 1)
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w v v order (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1), k.batch.day prorata ties by (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1)
kind lots: place one   min 0
  batched
  step 1
  takes k for w prorata
place konto: savings PLN lives 2026-01-01..
  note "the joint account"
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num = (if p == ania then 1 else 0) at m.day
  note "everything is ania's"
  note "a second note"
def a_part: money PLN = bal(konto, 2026-06-30) of ania at 2026-06-30
def b_part: money PLN = bal(konto, 2026-06-30)  of  (ania, w1) at 2026-06-30
def v_part: money PLN = value(konto, 2026-06-30) in PLN of ania at 2026-06-30
def l_part[m in events]: money PLN = (m.cash.amount of ania) / 2 at m.day

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  stated[konto] of ania = 10 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
  stated[konto] = 10 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
